And now imagine combining that procedural evidence with your existing voice embeddings, grammar measurements, speaking mechanics, and interaction profiles.

You can start using the structure of the meeting to help resolve ambiguous speaker boundaries rather than relying entirely on somebody's voice.

That's a substantially better-defined engineering problem than general-purpose speaker recognition.

